use std
into grow_test.amni

A test program for the `grow` library; imports math, vec, os, grow.grow, grow.forms and gfx.gltf. The library already provides, in namespace `grow`: `clear`, `seed`, `rnd`, `range`, `vcount`, `tcount`, `tube`, `phyllo`, `scatter`, `make`, `KINDS`, `open_edges`, `volume`, `bad_normals`, `digest`, `bounds`, `glb_bytes`, `glb`, `FORKS`, `S`, `I`, `GOLDEN` and `PI2`; and `gltf::load_bytes(data, dir) int` (an asset id, negative on failure), `gltf::reset()`, `gltf::assets`, `gltf::meshes`, `gltf::prims` (fields `vcount`, `icount`, `lo`, `hi` as float3) and `gltf::Span` (`at`, `len`). None of these may be defined here. A module counter `FAILS`; `check(ok, label)` (a bool and a read-only byte slice) prints "ok " or "FAIL " followed by the label and counts failures. `SEEDS` is 1, 7, 7177. `r3(x real) real` rounds to three decimals for printing.

`g1()`: for every kind in `grow::KINDS` and every seed, `make` it twice and compare `digest`s; check all equal ("G1 same seed, same mesh"). Then for every kind compare the digest at seed 7 with the one at seed 7177; check every kind differs ("G1 control: seed 7 vs 7177 differ").

`closed_tube(caps bool)` clears and builds a `tube` along five points (0, 0, 0), (0, 0.3, 0.07), (0.1, 0.7, 0.1), (0.3, 1, 0.1), (0.7, 1.2, 0) with radii 0.1, 0.09, 0.08, 0.07, 0.05, all colors white, 11 sides.

`g2_g3()`: for kinds "rock", "shell", "mushroom", "cactus" and "brain_coral" at every seed, record the largest `open_edges(0)`, the smallest `volume(0)` and the largest `bad_normals(0)`; then `closed_tube(true)` adds to the same three. Check open edges is 0 ("G2 closed solids"), then `closed_tube(false)` and check `open_edges(0)` is above 0 ("G2 control: uncapped tube is open"). Check the smallest volume is above 0 and bad normals is 0 ("G3 facing out, unit normals"). Also check `bad_normals(0)` is 0 for every kind at every seed ("G3 unit normals on every form"). Control: `make("rock", 7177, 1)`, swap the second and third id of every triangle in `grow::I`, check `volume(0)` is below 0 ("G3 control: flipped rock is negative"). Print each number.

`g4()`: for kinds "rock", "tree", "pine", "fern", "shell", "mushroom", "cactus", "coral" and "flower", seeds as above, size 1.7: the largest side of `bounds(0)`; record the worst ratio to 1.7 away from 1; print the kind and ratio of each; check every ratio is within 0.85 to 1.15 ("G4 asked size").

`g5()`: `phyllo(377, 1)`; the points are pairs in `grow::S`. For each consecutive pair of points the angle difference `atan2(z, x)` of the next minus this one, wrapped into [0, 2π), must equal `GOLDEN` wrapped the same way within 1e-9; check ("G5 phyllo steps 137.5078 degrees"). Nearest-neighbor distance of every point (all pairs), ratio of smallest to largest; print; check at least 0.47 ("G5 even packing"). Control: the same 377 points but stepping 90 degrees (radius `sqrt(i + 0.5)`, angle `i * π / 2`) gives a ratio under 0.47; print and check ("G5 control: 90 degree step clumps").

`g6()`: `seed(7177)`, `scatter(0, 0, 1, 37, 0.2)`; count points (pairs in S) and the smallest pair distance; check the smallest is at least 0.2 minus 1e-12 and the count at least 26 ("G6 scatter spacing"); print both. Control: 37 uniform random points in the same disc (radius `sqrt(rnd())`, angle `PI2 * rnd()`) have a smallest pair distance below 0.2; check ("G6 control: uniform random breaks spacing").

`g7()`: for kinds "tree", "bush" and "coral" at every seed, read `grow::FORKS` as pairs (parent end radius r, sum of children's squared start radii q); count forks and track the worst `|q - r * r| / (r * r)`; check forks exist and the worst is at most 0.02 ("G7 Leonardo's rule at every fork"); print forks and worst.

`g8()`: for every kind at seed 7177: `glb_bytes(out)`, `gltf::reset()`, `a = gltf::load_bytes(all of out, "")`; it must be at least 0; the asset's mesh's primitives (through `assets[a].meshes`, then `meshes[m].prims`) must be exactly one, with `vcount` equal to `vcount()`, `icount` equal to three times `tcount()`, and `lo` and `hi` equal to `bounds(0)` with each component converted to f32. Check all forms pass ("G8 GLB round trip"). Control: `gltf::reset()` and load only the first half of the last bytes; check the result is negative ("G8 control: half a file fails"). Also write `grow::glb` of the "fern" at seed 7177 to `/tmp/grow_fern.glb` only when the environment variable GROW_KEEP is set.

`BUDGET` pairs each kind with its triangle limit: rock 2700, shell 7000, mushroom 4700, cactus 7000, succulent 4700, flower 4700, tuft 700, tree 27000, pine 27000, bush 17000, fern 7700, coral 17000, brain_coral 7000, moss 7000. `g9_g10()`: for every kind print its name, vertices and triangles at seed 7177, the best of three build times (`time_ns` around `make`) in milliseconds with two decimals, and its budget; check every kind at every seed stays within budget ("G9 phone budget") and every best time is under 20 ms ("G10 speed").

`main()`: when the program's arguments are `--glb kind seed size out`, `make` that kind (exit 2 with a message for an unknown kind), write it with `glb` and print the vertex and triangle counts; otherwise run g1 to g10 and print "grow: ok", or "grow: FAILED " and the count and exit 1.
